\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Paired evaluation separates reference resolution, ranking resolution and restriction quality. (a) The selection budget $W$ and ranking tolerance $\tau $ determine the finite-world reference and the top-$q$ pool $C(\tau ,q)$. Both arms share the graph, world prefix, seed budget and tie rule. (b) Shared evaluation worlds, independent of selection, yield the utility difference $\Delta U$. Set agreement $J$ and selection-cost ratio $\rho _T$ complete the quality--cost comparison.}}{3}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:evaluation-mechanism}{{1}{3}{Paired evaluation separates reference resolution, ranking resolution and restriction quality. (a) The selection budget $W$ and ranking tolerance $\tau $ determine the finite-world reference and the top-$q$ pool $C(\tau ,q)$. Both arms share the graph, world prefix, seed budget and tie rule. (b) Shared evaluation worlds, independent of selection, yield the utility difference $\Delta U$. Set agreement $J$ and selection-cost ratio $\rho _T$ complete the quality--cost comparison}{figure.1}{}}
