\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Budget and ranking precision have distinct effects on candidate-restriction quality. Points are mean incremental losses over five paired paths; bars are path standard deviations. Default and strict tolerances are $10^{-6}$ and $10^{-12}$, with strict pools stable at $10^{-14}$. Negative loss favors the restricted set. The ca-GrQc default reversal disappears under strict ranking, while the directed-network losses persist. This is a post-hoc paired sensitivity analysis.}}{9}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:precision-budget}{{2}{9}{Budget and ranking precision have distinct effects on candidate-restriction quality. Points are mean incremental losses over five paired paths; bars are path standard deviations. Default and strict tolerances are $10^{-6}$ and $10^{-12}$, with strict pools stable at $10^{-14}$. Negative loss favors the restricted set. The ca-GrQc default reversal disappears under strict ranking, while the directed-network losses persist. This is a post-hoc paired sensitivity analysis}{figure.2}{}}
